      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- **Before any file is overwritten**, the guarded tool executor first records that file\u0027s previous state \u2014 either its prior content (if it existed) or a marker that it did not exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n- **If a run fails** (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed before, and deleting newly created files.\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This approach provides transaction-like guarantees for writes without needing a database \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held in memory for the duration of one run.\n- **Query agent exception**: The Query agent (which is what you\u0027re speaking with now) never uses this rollback path, since it has no write tool \u2014 the journal only gets populated by agents that actually perform writes.",
